        "statement": "On R2 x [0,L], define full 3D critical Abelian-Higgs static energy with fixed flux 2pi n on each transverse slice, no radial flux leakage, uniform vacuum approach and the angular one-form condition. For fixed smooth finite-energy end traces in the same canonical exterior gauge, prove exterior phase cleanup and L2 differences from one selected arbitrary-divisor planar minimizer; construct smooth fixed-width linear-interpolation collars of finite energy C0,C1 independent of L. Then prove T_n L<=inf E_L<=T_n(L-2ell)+C0+C1 with T_n=2pi xi |n|; in particular inf E_L=T_n L+O(1). Matching minimizing traces give an exact translation-invariant minimum. Keep this a mathematical fixed-flux boundary variational statement, not point-source self-energy or a quantum Wilson-loop claim.",
