        "title": "Taubes disk barriers and monotone Dirichlet iteration",
        "statement": "For any finite planar divisor and kappa>0, prove explicit global logarithmic subsolution u_minus=sum m_j log(r_j²/(r_j²+lambda)) for lambda>=4n/kappa. On each containing disk construct singular Dirichlet Green u_sing, supersolution u_sing+psi with Delta psi=-kappa, and prove ordering. After singular subtraction v, use the positive (-Delta+L) Dirichlet resolver to prove monotone convergence to a smooth solution of -Delta v+kappa(exp(u_sing+v)-1)=0 with zero outer boundary. Prove maximum principle u<=0, uniform local bounds after a fixed singular subtraction, and the exact elliptic estimates needed for an exhausting-disk subsequence. Avoid unnecessary unproved exponential-functional/Trudinger coercivity assumptions.",
        "reference": "items/lem-qftx-taubes-disk-barriers-and-monotone-iteration.md#Statement",
        "design_state": "Planned prerequisite: Statement/Definition contract only. Native author must supply complete local proof/source review before readiness; no acceptance, retrieval or proof stamp is implied.",
        "proof_design": "For disk radius R containing all z_j, use u_sing(z)=sum m_j log(R²|z-z_j|²/|R²-conj(z_j)z|²), A_R=exp(u_sing) smooth nonnegative, psi=kappa(R²-|z|²)/4. Choose L>=kappa max A_R exp(psi); (-Delta+L) inverse positive by maximum principle. Iterate T(v)=(-Delta+L)^-1[kappa+Lv-kappa A_R exp(v)] between lower u_minus-u_sing and upper psi. Monotone RHS derivative nonnegative; bound u_R<=0 by maximum principle. For exhaustion, subtract fixed u_minus, not R-dependent u_sing: on each compact disk its regular difference has bounded Laplacian and bounded boundary values, so local bounds survive R->infinity. Obtain n=2 W2p and Schauder compactness with exact supplier hypotheses; prove regularity at centers and derivative decay before claiming finite energy.",
